sgi-replay 2
head sgi-mgras
# One row of mandel's first rectwrite, cut from the IRIX 6.5.30 session
# a captured run (mandel from the 6.5.12 demos, IRIS GL
# through the IGLOO libgl.so, on the SI): the context switch to its
# context 0x5420, then every main-port word up to the end of the first
# pixel draw. Kept: the port, context and flag-clear writes; dropped: reads,
# the cursor, DAC and retrace writes around them. Added: the handshake's
# first two lines, as fill.replay has them, and the context's 0x0a04 12,
# which the session sent when it set the context up, long before this
# switch.
#
# The draw: the program 0x1a3e, 0x352d (colour indices), the rectangle
# 0, 0 to 99, 0 at 0xe34, zoom 1, then 0x8d20 with 50 words a row and one
# inline block of 100 big-endian 16-bit indices. The window's lower-left
# pixel is (96, 828) counted from the bottom (context word 2, 0x033c0060),
# so the row lands on screen row 195, columns 96 to 195, and each index
# keeps all twelve bits, as a 12-bit context's pixel does. The row above
# keeps index 8, the clear index the context's glClear (0xbd04, 0x1500
# above) left. The rectangle is the
# image's own; the GE places it at the raster position, which mandel's
# glRasterPos2i (0x58003808, 0, 0 above) puts at the centre of the
# window's corner pixel through its projection (0x2b40 above). That
# lands at 0.500003, not 0.5; the model's snap to 1/256 pixel keeps the
# row on the corner pixel.
